Graham asks: Is refinement egraph concepts supplied by egg / egglog analyses. I'm inclinced to say no.

A canonical example is a set algebra

https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Algebra_of_sets
https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_set_identities_and_relations

```
(fun U (+ +)) ; union
(fun I (+ +))
(fun diff (+ -)) ; set difference is anti-monotone in second arg


(rewrite (U ?a ?b) (U ?b ?a))  ; in
(lte A B) ;; assert A is less than equal to B
()

(refine (I ?a ?b)  ?a) ; intersection is less than 
(antirefine (U ?a ?b) ?a))   ; a better name? refine- or generalize or ..? Union is

(rewrite )  ; equality

; Any nice syntax to combine refine antirefine and rewrite?
; ?a- ?a= ?a+   to allow matching above and below
; ( ) equality subterm {} all terms below [] all terms above?
; So that using () gives you the usual.
```

